{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792944882,"nonce":"SoqdHzSaYa1aiQsHIJNPfa/0Fy0=","title":"wasm: try/catch never catches; lower the setjmp handler pattern to wasm exception handling","message":"MIR lowers try/catch as `rayzor_exception_push_handler()` + `_setjmp(buf)` with a branch to the landing pad on a nonzero result, and `throw` as `rayzor_throw_typed`, which longjmps natively.\n\nOn wasm there is no setjmp. runtime-wasm/src/exceptions.rs makes `_setjmp` return 0 and keeps only a handler depth; `rayzor_throw_typed` prints \"uncaught exception\" and traps. So a try body runs, and any throw — including one inside a try — kills the instance. `rayzor_get_exception*` return 0.\n\nFix belongs in wasm_backend (not MIR): recognise the push_handler/_setjmp/branch shape and emit a wasm EH `try_table` whose catch target is the landing pad, with `rayzor_throw_typed` becoming a `throw` of a module tag carrying (value, type_id). wasmtime 48 supports the exception-handling proposal; the runner must enable it. runtime-wasm then needs current-exception state for rayzor_get_exception/_type_id, and rayzor_exception_type_matches needs the class hierarchy (it checks only equality and interface impls today).","files":null}]}